{{also|bucherei}}
==German==

===Etymology===
A calque of {{der|de|la|librāria}}, possibly through {{der|de|nl|boekerij}}, which seems to be slightly older. Analyzable as {{suffix|de|Bücher|t1=books|-ei}} or {{suffix|de|Buch|t1=book|-erei}}, ultimately translatable as "[[bookery]]".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˌbyːçəˈʁaɪ̯/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Bücherei.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|aɪ̯|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|old=1}}

# [[library]]
#: {{syn|de|Bibliothek}}

====Usage notes====
* The word is typically used only for town libraries or private libraries, while university libraries are generally called ''Bibliothek''.

